dotfiles
========

This repository is used to store my configuration files with a quick
installation guide for my personal needs.

How it works
------------

The `install.sh` script symlinks each file of this repository into your home
directory at the same relative path.

For example, `.ssh/config` is linked as `~/.ssh/config`, so any change to the
configuration is tracked by this repository.

Existing files in your home directory are replaced by the symbolic links.

Installation
------------

1. Clone this repository:

    ```bash
    git clone git@github.com:hugofresnel/dotfiles.git && cd dotfiles
    ```

2. Run installation script to create symbolic links in your home directory:

    ```bash
    ./install.sh
    ```

Windows / WSL
-------------

When using Windows + WSL, run `install.ps1` from an Administrator PowerShell
terminal to create symbolic links to the WSL configuration files:

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass .\install.ps1
```
